record with 69.00 (226-4½), which was the third best throw ever. That would eventually stand up for the gold medal. Bulgaria’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/65708"} "Mariya Vergova"] " moved into second in round two with 67.30 (220-9¾) and would win the silver medal. Melnik was a strange non-factor for the gold, and failed to medal.On her fifth throw Melnik was warned by a judge that she was taking too long to complete her throw. The pair got into an argument and eventually the judge reversed his decision. Visibly angered Melnik channelled her aggression and threw  the discus to within half a metre of the lead. However the throw was later declared void. Poland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/74645"} "Danuta Rosani"] " qualified for the final but before she could compete, was disqualified for doping when her sample showed an anabolic steroid. This was the first Olympic doping positive in track &amp; field athletics."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "157"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/69729"} "Evelin Schlaak"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GDR.png"}] "GDR"]] [:td {} "61.86 (4)"] [:td {} "69.00 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "54"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/65708"} "Mariya Vergova"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BUL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/BUL.png"}] "BUL"]] [:td {} "57.96 (10)"] [:td {} "67.30 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]]